.TH FLUTTER-RUNNER 1 "October 2024" "1.0" "Flutter Runner Manual"
.SH NAME
flutter-runner \- A script to build and run Flutter apps for iOS and Android.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flutter-runner
[\-r platform] [\-b platform] [\-e extra_flags]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flutter-runner
automates the process of building and running Flutter applications for iOS and Android platforms. It manages platform-specific tasks, including moving problematic files, excluding dependencies, and modifying specific files before building or running the app.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r platform
Run the app on the specified platform. Valid values are:
.RS
.IP
**ios**: Runs the app on an iOS device or simulator.
.IP
**android**: Runs the app on an Android device or emulator.
.RE

.TP
.B \-b platform
Build the app for the specified platform. Valid values are:
.RS
.IP
**ios**: Builds the app for iOS.
.IP
**android**: Builds the app for Android.
.RE

.TP
.B \-e extra_flags
Specify additional flags to pass to the Flutter command. This can be used to customize the build or run process.

.SH EXAMPLES
Run the app on iOS:
.RS
.nf
flutter-runner -r ios
.fi
.RE

Build the app for Android:
.RS
.nf
flutter-runner -b android
.fi
.RE

Run the app on Android with additional flags:
.RS
.nf
flutter-runner -r android -e "--flavor production"
.fi
.RE

.SH FILES
.B pubspec.yaml
Used to specify iOS-specific ignored files, ignored dependencies, and files to modify.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
Requires Flutter SDK to be installed and in the system PATH. For iOS builds, requires Xcode and CocoaPods. For Android builds, requires the Android SDK.

.SH NOTES
The script uses .B yq for YAML parsing. Ensure it is installed and accessible in the PATH.

.SH SEE ALSO
.B flutter(1), pod(1), yq(1)

